  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "071f7f0685872175acab87457561286bb24d196c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 613704388,
          "type": null,
          "body": "ui/qt/import_text_dialog.cpp does:\n\n```\n#if defined(_WIN32)\n            // At least some Windows C libraries have this.\n            // Some UN*X C libraries do, as well, but they might not\n            // show it unless you're requesting C11 - or C++17.\n            timespec_get(&timenow, TIME_UTC);\n#elif defined(HAVE_CLOCK_GETTIME)\n            // Newer POSIX API.  Some UN*Xes whose C libraries lack\n            // timespec_get() (C11) have this.\n            clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, &timenow);\n#else\n            // Fall back on gettimeofday().\n            struct timeval usectimenow;\n            gettimeofday(&usectimenow, NULL);\n            timenow.tv_sec = usectimenow.tv_sec;\n            timenow.tv_nsec = usectimenow.tv_usec*1000;\n#endif\n```\n\nShould there be a single routine in wsutil to get seconds/nanoseconds time?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-29T00:15:33.695Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-29T00:15:33.695Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 106174573,
