    {
      "id": "79ee7596169af63ba34a27ec46b5c33f46636d1b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 613807041,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> I didn't know of text import. It could use an IPv6 makeover.\n\nIt could also use a merger of its code and text2pcap.c.\n\n> For wslog the code is so small and trivial and there an (intentional) semantic difference with tv_nsec that I would not bother with that.\n\nIf you mean \"`tv_nsec` is a `long int` in a `ws_log_time_t`\", [it's also a `long int` in a POSIX `struct timespec`](https://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/time.h.html) and in the `struct timespec` in at least some versions of the Microsoft Universal CRT, so presumably *that's* not the semantic difference, unless I'm missing something.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-06-29T05:42:56.519Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-06-29T05:42:56.519Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 106174573,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
